okay so spider-man now at home build  upon the last 20 years of the sony  spider-verse to bring us a film that  broke the mcu in order to make one of  the biggest events in comic book movie  history seeing andrew garfield and toby  maguire appear on screen together  alongside tom holland was something that  we never thought could happen but marvel  delivered this massive event to make it  the highest grossing film this side of  the pandemic i hadn't felt that hype  since jay-z and naz appeared on stage  together during the i declare war tour  and it's still something that gives me  goosebumps every time i watch it  i know you can feel the magic baby  what i think of the film excel that  though was giving andrew garfield's  peter parker a much deserved redemption  arc when you hear everything that went  on behind the scenes with him it's not  difficult to feel sorry for the actor  and when he played the character he had  several things riding against him the  amazing spider-man released in 2012 just  five years after toby mcguire appeared  as peter parker in spider-man 3. the  amazing spider-man 2 dropped two years  later in 2014 and it would be a mere two  years after that in which he was  replaced by tom holland in a complete  reboot of the character garfield was  actually due to announce the amazing  spider-man 3 at a brazilian comic book  movie event but he called in sick and  then the project was scrapped it was  only after the sony email hack that we  found out amy pascal had been in talks  with kevin feige to reboot the character  in the mcu and garfield's version was  swept into the rug by the studio online  though there was still a massive  community that supported him and just in  the same way that the snyder cut had  several people writing for it garfield  did too thus seeing him back on the big  screen alongside toby and tom was a  major moment that not only righted the  wrongs of the past but it also showed  the growth of the character for the last  decade lots of people have argued who  the best live-action spider-man is and  after seeing them on screen at the same  time i actually think that garfield is  by far the standout in my opinion he  swings circles around the other two and  it's easy to see why he's had such a  massive career outside of this franchise  now not only does the film give  redemption to garfield but it also gives  redemption to his version of peter  parker the amazing spider-man 2 ended  with the love of his life gwen stacy  falling to her death and after he  misused his webs he ended up breaking  her neck it's arguably one of the most  tragic moments in the spider-man movie  ever and though the death of uncle ben  and may are definitely up there this  hits a lot harder because it was caused  somewhat directly by him in the movie we  discovered that this very much broke the  character and then after the death of  gwen he stopped pulling his punches  i lost gwen my um  she was my mj  some point i just  i stopped pulling my punches  this took him down a darker path in  which he became more vengeful and less  forgiving he'd seen firsthand that even  when you try and do good that it can  still lead to loss and had just stopped  giving the villains the benefit of the  doubt like he had in his past now a  theme that's very prevalent in no way  home is the idea of responsibility the  two of the peters that tom's version  meets very much act as a warning in the  wake of ant-may's death not only did  andrew losing gwen make him go down a  darker path but we also see how  something similar happened with toby's  peter he recounts and either uncle ben  died and though he says he managed to  stop the quote-unquote killer it didn't  make him feel better it didn't make it  better  it took me a long time to  learn to get through that darkness  otobi very much saves tom's version from  receiving this same fate in the movie we  watch as the green goblin kills aunt may  and come the final battle peter  completely beats the crap out of him  just in the same way that toby led to  the death of his apparent uncle's killer  tom is about to do the same thing and  finally get revenge on the person that  killed the parental figure in his life  also side note i have to keep saying the  guy who apparently killed uncle ben  because of that stupid sandman retcon  but yeah to me it'll always be this guy  who did it anyway it's a great moment  watching toby stop tom from shoving the  glider into the goblin which is of  course also the way that he died in the  original film it's a very heroic moment  that stops him from becoming vengeful  and filled with anger however the way  that andrew spares him from this path is  far more subtle and he not only saves  tom's soul but also his own after  osborne arrives at the statue of liberty  he hurts goblin bombs and he destroys  the scaffolding holding the structure in  place this causes the entire thing to  collapse and during this destruction mj  falls to her death much in the same way  that gwen did tom's peter leaps out to  grab her but the goblin catches in  mid-air stopping him from saving the  girl that he loves much in the same way  that comics have shown the goblin  killing the person he loves over and  over it seems like history is repeating  itself and this is made even worse by  the fact that osborne also killed may  however andrew's version leaps after her  and he ends up breaking her fall which  in turn saves her life just in the same  way that toby stopped him from traveling  down this dark path due to him killing  his aunt's killer andrew has stopped him  from going down the same one he did  after losing his love he even refers to  mj as his gwen at one point and andrew  carrying this out here also saves  another person from suffering the same  fate that she did rather than using a  web to latch onto her he takes the  impact himself and this shows that he  hasn't made the same mistake it's a  really powerful moment and andrew  completely axes ass off as mj asks him  if he's okay  are you okay  yeah  okay  are you okay  now even though we all watched the  second trailer about 500 times and  figured out that this moment was coming  it still hits home so hard that's the  power of the movie and it showcases that  even when things are telegraphed that  they can still be impactful due to the  performance and also what it means for  the character and actor it's so well  done and it makes you truly see the  impact of exactly what his peter is  going through it saves tom's version  much in the same way that toby stopped  him from killing the goblin and it  spares him from being a spider-man that  refuses to pull his punches the movie is  very much about serving the villains and  throughout it we see as peter does this  even when it's the more difficult choice  however it's also about saving peter as  well and stopping him from becoming  someone that his elder versions wish  they hadn't changed into it's such  amazing storytelling and this scene only  works on a number of levels because of  what it means for the character but also  the actor behind it for fans garfield no  longer feels like he was robbed of  playing the character that he was  obsessed over as a kid but instead we  can leave the film knowing that he  finally got the opportunity to be  clashed shoulder-to-shoulder with the  more favored people that have played him  where we go from here we don't know but  i really hope that the rumblings about  garfield returning are indeed true  whether it's in venom 3 or his own  spin-off movie i think he's someone that  really shines in this film and it shows  that when he's given the right material  he can be the perfect peter parker  watching his two solo films and nowhere  home tied into it really brings his arc  to a close but from this point on there  are several directions that they could  take things we know that he hasn't found  someone after gwen left the hole in his  life and though that may never be filled  i think we all just want to see the guy  happy all in all though that's a story  for another day and after re-watching  the movie knowing what this moment means  to the actor and the character i don't  think that it's anything other than  perfect i'd of course love to hear your  thoughts whether you agree whether you  disagree so make sure you comment below  and let me know we are in a competition  right now and giving away three copies  of an mc box that we chose on the 30th  of january and all you have to do to be  on the chance of winning is like the  video make sure you subscribe with  notifications on and drop a comment  below with your thoughts on the video we  pick the comments at random at the end  of the month and the winners of the last  one on screen right now so that's you  then message me on twitter at  heavyspoilers if you want something else  to watch then make sure you check our  video in which we break down andrew  garfield's interview about spiderman  nowy home finally gets to talk about it  and all the things that went into the  movie so definitely go check it out  right after this if not then thanks for  sticking through the video i've been  poor i'll see you on the next one take  care peace

